---
fiscal_year_starts: july
---

# FY2026 Budget: Quarterly Engineering Spend

An Australian SaaS company allocates its $4.8M annual engineering budget across fiscal quarters. The fiscal year runs July through June.

## Annual Budget

annual_eng_budget = $4,800,000
quarterly_budget = $4,800,000 / 4

## Fiscal Quarter Dates

fq1_start = FQ1
fq1_end = end of FQ1
fq2_start = FQ2
fq2_end = end of FQ2
fq3_start = FQ3
fq3_end = end of FQ3
fq4_start = FQ4
fq4_end = end of FQ4

## Daily Run Rates

Same budget, different day counts per quarter:

fq1_daily = quarterly_budget / (FQ1 in days)
fq2_daily = quarterly_budget / (FQ2 in days)
fq3_daily = quarterly_budget / (FQ3 in days)
fq4_daily = quarterly_budget / (FQ4 in days)

## Calendar vs. Fiscal

Calendar Q3 = Fiscal Q1 with a July fiscal year:

cal_q3 = Q3
fiscal_q1 = FQ1

## Fiscal Year Boundaries

fy_start = this fiscal year
fy_end = end of this fiscal year

## Leap Year Impact

Compare FQ3 (Jan-Mar) across leap and non-leap years:

fy24_fq3 = Apr 1 2024 - Jan 1 2024
fy25_fq3 = Apr 1 2025 - Jan 1 2025
leap_difference = Apr 1 2024 - Jan 1 2024 - (Apr 1 2025 - Jan 1 2025)

## Mid-Quarter Reforecast

14 days into FQ2:

fq2_elapsed = 14
fq2_per_day = quarterly_budget / number(FQ2 in days)
fq2_spent = fq2_per_day * fq2_elapsed
fq2_remaining = quarterly_budget - fq2_spent

## Contractor Ramp

A contractor team starts mid-FQ3 (Jan-Mar) and ramps over 45 days. How many full days remain in FQ3 after ramp?

contractor_start = Jan 15 2025
ramp_end = contractor_start + 45 days
fq3_end_date = Mar 31 2025
full_rate_days = fq3_end_date - ramp_end
days_in_fq3 = FQ3 in days

## Key Dates

board_review = FQ3 + 15 days
budget_lock = end of this fiscal year - 2 weeks
